     "date": "2026-03-11T07:45:04Z"
    },
    "message": "fix(git): quick diff and blame break for worktrees inside bare repos\n\nWhen a bare repository is used as the common git directory and worktrees\nare stored as subdirectories inside it (e.g. repo.git/work/), the\n`dotGit.commonPath` equals the bare repo root, which is an ancestor of\nthe worktree root. The isDescendant guard in provideOriginalResource was\nevaluating to true for every source file in those worktrees, causing it\nto return undefined for all of them.\n\nThis made TextEditor.diffInformation undefined for all files in such\nworktrees, which prevented quick diff gutter decorations, inline blame,\nstatus bar blame, and stage-hunk from working.\n\nFix by additionally checking that the file is not inside repository.root\n(the working tree), unless the git dir is itself inside repository.root\n(the standard case where .git/ is a subdirectory of the repo root).\n\nFixes: bare repo + nested worktree pattern used with \"git worktree add\"",
